* sg13g2-pll :: sim/sg13cmos5l-postlayout-pex-pvt (issue #30, Part of #16)
* SCHEMATIC-LEVEL control arm for the post-layout comparison.
*
* This is ../../sg13cmos5l-vco-kvco-table/testbench/tb_vco_kvco.sp.tmpl with
* exactly ONE deliberate difference: `.tran`'s stop time is 30n rather than
* 40n, matching the post-layout arm so both arms are solved over an identical
* window. The measurement itself (`per1`, between the 3rd and 4th rising edge
* of CLK) is a steady-state period and is reached well inside 30 ns on every
* corner of this matrix -- the slowest committed schematic period is 2.25 ns,
* and the slowest post-layout period measured by this record is under 4 ns, so
* the 4th rising edge lands near 17 ns at worst. The shortened window is a
* runtime measure for the post-layout arm (whose 170 extracted parasitic
* resistors and 344 parasitic capacitors make each transient roughly 15x more
* expensive), applied to BOTH arms so it cannot bias the comparison. That this
* arm still reproduces the committed 40 ns-window results is checked
* explicitly -- see ../records/RECORD-001, "Does the control arm reproduce the
* committed campaign?".
*
* Everything else -- corner libraries, `.option scale=1`, the ideal DC sources
* on VCTRL/B0/B1/VDD_VCO, the XCDECAP-stripped netlist derivation, the
* symmetry-breaking `.ic`, and the `.meas` line -- is byte-for-byte the
* original campaign's.

.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerMOShv.lib @CORNER_MOS@
.lib @PDK_ROOT@/@PDK@/libs.tech/ngspice/models/cornerRES.lib @CORNER_RES@
.option scale=1 temp=@TEMP@
.global sub!

.include vco_open.spice

Vvctrl vctrl 0 dc @VCTRL@
Vb0 b0 0 dc @B0V@
Vb1 b1 0 dc @B1V@
Vdd vdd 0 dc 3.3
Vsub sub! 0 dc 0

Xvco vctrl b0 b1 clk vdd 0 vco

.ic v(xvco.ring1)=0.5

.tran 20p 30n

.control
run
meas tran per1 trig v(clk) val=1.65 rise=3 targ v(clk) val=1.65 rise=4
print per1
.endc
.end
